            {
                "entry_id": "c5646e91-b571-3516-837d-8d8fd9dd7dca",
                "word": "menée",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8d2e4902-fba2-4e4c-b21b-44ab443fe6be",
                        "entry_id": "c5646e91-b571-3516-837d-8d8fd9dd7dca",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "menées"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79ff3ed9-bf6f-3298-9c87-6bdd591d2a44",
                        "entry_id": "c5646e91-b571-3516-837d-8d8fd9dd7dca",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pratique secrète et artificieuse dont on se sert pour faire réussir un projet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Surtout au pluriel"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d3cca563-eebd-4ec5-ba60-391f60a672ba",
                                "sense_id": "79ff3ed9-bf6f-3298-9c87-6bdd591d2a44",
                                "text": "La veille du jour où il arrêta Eugène sur le cours Sauvaire, il avait publié, dans l’Indépendant, un article terrible sur les menées du clergé, en réponse à un entrefilet de Vuillet, qui accusait les républicains de vouloir démolir les églises."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "36cee792-9df4-43aa-b08c-e71b3f794efc",
                                "sense_id": "79ff3ed9-bf6f-3298-9c87-6bdd591d2a44",
                                "text": "Quant au duc d’Orléans, il jouissait de peu de popularité et de peu d’influence. C’était l’homme des petites menées ; il rabaissait à sa taille les choses dont il s’occupait."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c38ea4f5-fa12-41ac-80d1-c1da28f26065",
                                "sense_id": "79ff3ed9-bf6f-3298-9c87-6bdd591d2a44",
                                "text": "Le dit gouvernement avait déjà eu vent de la participation de Bakounine aux menées révolutionnaires."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "97601ee0-4a95-4173-acad-3b007708edea",
                                "sense_id": "79ff3ed9-bf6f-3298-9c87-6bdd591d2a44",
                                "text": "Or, cette année-là, comme les élections étaient fixées au 1ᵉʳ mai, il y eut dès le 1ᵉʳ avril, une propagande active et des menées sourdes de part et d’autre pour conquérir les douteux."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5200a928-9a53-3c0f-993a-e9633fd1c5d0",
                        "entry_id": "c5646e91-b571-3516-837d-8d8fd9dd7dca",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Route suivie par une bête en fuite, en particulier un cerf."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7baf013b-a2cc-4710-b5a2-89a2af1231be",
                                "sense_id": "5200a928-9a53-3c0f-993a-e9633fd1c5d0",
                                "text": "Suivre la menée, être à la menée de la bête."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3a1e712a-d066-369a-ba29-d9b1fc87774a",
                        "entry_id": "c5646e91-b571-3516-837d-8d8fd9dd7dca",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Congère."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "35f12af4-c2ae-41e3-9075-528abca84182",
                                "sense_id": "3a1e712a-d066-369a-ba29-d9b1fc87774a",
                                "text": "La neige […] formant de véritables dunes blanches, des « menées » qui se déplaçaient rapidement sous l'effort du vent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "26c35334-7665-41d5-88a0-a840fd9ed455",
                        "source_entry_id": "c5646e91-b571-3516-837d-8d8fd9dd7dca",
                        "target_lang_word": "tendency",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tendency",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af9b5d84-2ba4-3dc2-975f-2ed35bd1ae7e",
                                        "entry_id": "24c45fd7-7c82-3c92-b9e4-d15b01766ebc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A likelihood of behaving in a particular way or going in a particular direction; a tending toward."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4deeed7a-8845-4c8f-981f-7163062e1e47",
                                                "sense_id": "af9b5d84-2ba4-3dc2-975f-2ed35bd1ae7e",
                                                "text": "Denim has a tendency to fade."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02962f1c-1f9d-46ba-932c-0d3801fa2e59",
                                                "sense_id": "af9b5d84-2ba4-3dc2-975f-2ed35bd1ae7e",
                                                "text": "I have a tendency to get bored after the first half an hour of a movie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c4ffd0b-20cd-43c4-8021-015812ed41e1",
                                                "sense_id": "af9b5d84-2ba4-3dc2-975f-2ed35bd1ae7e",
                                                "text": "There's a common tendency among first-game visitors to a casino to bet overcautiously."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34feefbb-3b3f-4689-b941-c4b7c2641ffa",
                                                "sense_id": "af9b5d84-2ba4-3dc2-975f-2ed35bd1ae7e",
                                                "text": "In some details, Britannia shows the trend towards American practice that was already apparent in later L.M.S.R. designs—for example, in regard to the mounting of the cab—and this tendency has been further developed in the footwalk with deep sideplating, mounted on the boiler, in place of the framing and splashers usual in British practice in the past."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f87df18-1dbd-3bc1-9b71-75de1190f169",
                                        "entry_id": "24c45fd7-7c82-3c92-b9e4-d15b01766ebc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An organised unit or faction within a larger political organisation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d752205a-cc1c-4ed0-b070-41e36077d419",
                                                "sense_id": "9f87df18-1dbd-3bc1-9b71-75de1190f169",
                                                "text": "Mao launched the struggle against the vulgar materialist tendency within the party as early as 1937."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "099d7751-ab0c-4928-826a-678ffe76ed1e",
                                                "sense_id": "9f87df18-1dbd-3bc1-9b71-75de1190f169",
                                                "text": "In stark contrast to the Europeanist tendency within the party and the Suez Group, this group had a short history."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af05b38f-5e49-42eb-80aa-59e97b1d7311",
                                                "sense_id": "9f87df18-1dbd-3bc1-9b71-75de1190f169",
                                                "text": "It reinforced the position of the conformist tendency within the party, since the majority of the candidates were old politicians, many of them members of Papandreou's centre-left CU faction back in the mid-1960s."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
